            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-53632",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "launch-editor: launch-editor: Credential compromise via NTLMv2 password hash leak through UNC path access"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "launch-editor allows users to open files with line numbers in editor from Node.js. Prior to 2.14.1, the launch-editor NPM package accesses arbitrary paths including Windows UNC paths. When a UNC path is opened, Windows automatically attempts NTLM authentication to the remote host, causing the user’s NTLMv2 password hash to be leaked to an attacker-controlled SMB server. This can result in credential compromise through offline hash cracking. This vulnerability is fixed in 2.14.1."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-53632",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-53632\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: launch-editor\nFixed Version: 2.14.1\nLink: [CVE-2026-53632](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-53632)\nlaunch-editor allows users to open files with line numbers in editor from Node.js. Prior to 2.14.1, the launch-editor NPM package accesses arbitrary paths including Windows UNC paths. When a UNC path is opened, Windows automatically attempts NTLM authentication to the remote host, causing the user’s NTLMv2 password hash to be leaked to an attacker-controlled SMB server. This can result in credential compromise through offline hash cracking. This vulnerability is fixed in 2.14.1.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-53632**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|launch-editor|2.14.1|[CVE-2026-53632](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-53632)|\n\nlaunch-editor allows users to open files with line numbers in editor from Node.js. Prior to 2.14.1, the launch-editor NPM package accesses arbitrary paths including Windows UNC paths. When a UNC path is opened, Windows automatically attempts NTLM authentication to the remote host, causing the user’s NTLMv2 password hash to be leaked to an attacker-controlled SMB server. This can result in credential compromise through offline hash cracking. This vulnerability is fixed in 2.14.1."
