            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-7339",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "on-headers: on-headers vulnerable to http response header manipulation"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "on-headers is a node.js middleware for listening to when a response writes headers. A bug in on-headers versions `\u003c1.1.0` may result in response headers being inadvertently modified when an array is passed to `response.writeHead()`. Users should upgrade to version 1.1.0 to receive a patch. Uses are strongly encouraged to upgrade to `1.1.0`, but this issue can be worked around by passing an object to `response.writeHead()` rather than an array."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-7339",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-7339\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: on-headers\nFixed Version: 1.1.0\nLink: [CVE-2025-7339](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-7339)\non-headers is a node.js middleware for listening to when a response writes headers. A bug in on-headers versions `\u003c1.1.0` may result in response headers being inadvertently modified when an array is passed to `response.writeHead()`. Users should upgrade to version 1.1.0 to receive a patch. Uses are strongly encouraged to upgrade to `1.1.0`, but this issue can be worked around by passing an object to `response.writeHead()` rather than an array.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-7339**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|on-headers|1.1.0|[CVE-2025-7339](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-7339)|\n\non-headers is a node.js middleware for listening to when a response writes headers. A bug in on-headers versions `\u003c1.1.0` may result in response headers being inadvertently modified when an array is passed to `response.writeHead()`. Users should upgrade to version 1.1.0 to receive a patch. Uses are strongly encouraged to upgrade to `1.1.0`, but this issue can be worked around by passing an object to `response.writeHead()` rather than an array."
